item.stdout:
# ADR 0042: Captured working-tree preselection

Status: implementation decision; correctness and release gates remain separate.

## Context

P1 diagnosis found that extraction reuse bypassed Git's bounded preliminary
candidate pool. Equal worktrees consequently selected different files. Restoring
Git's live content scan would violate the operation's single-observation contract.
A first Go-only replacement also missed Git binary attributes and caller-locale
behavior. These were correctness findings, not performance-tuning opportunities.

## Decision

Observe fixed-pattern matches while the confined descriptor is read for capture.
The observer sees oversized tails during the existing digest pass; it retains
query-term presence, a bounded match window and a matching-line budget, not the
oversized body. Parser limits remain unchanged. Retain a matched-file marker even
when a matching substring has no normalized query-term contribution, preserving
the preliminary pool's existing behavior. Later query stages cannot enable live
Git content reads in captured mode.

Alias-aware search replays the same bounded scan plan as ordinary preselection:
one 32-line ordinary-term pass, then either one 32-line coalesced-alias pass or
one first-line pass per independent alias. A single line reducer distributes all
query-term bits from each retained matching line to those passes. Its buffer is
bounded by the operation's configured input limit; a physical line above that
limit fails captured preselection explicitly rather than truncating evidence.
Conservative Unicode boundary matches validate against the already captured
file. That full-file fallback records all query terms even when it confirms no
alias, matching the ordinary Git callback's existing saturation behavior.

Use Git to evaluate attributes in an ephemeral attribute-only worktree. Populate
it from captured ancestor `.gitattributes` bytes. For absent worktree policies,
freeze the index's stage-0 blob identity and read that immutable blob. Materialize
empty placeholders when neither observation supplies a policy. Git never reads
source bodies in this step. Keep automatic binary sniffing distinct from forced
binary and forced text, including custom driver settings. Enforce aggregate
policy/output bounds and validate repository metadata before invoking Git.

Retain the first effective attribute decision per path in the operation store,
and include the decision digest in operation input identity. Provider-owned
policy bytes share source capture. Git's other listing/configuration/metadata
probes remain an explicit opaque coverage boundary; no atomic repository claim
or persistent working-tree snapshot is introduced.

C/POSIX matching folds ASCII only. Other locale matching currently uses Go's
Unicode simple folding; discriminating fixtures cover C, POSIX and one available
UTF-8 locale. This evidence does not establish equivalence for every locale or
platform. Repository-subdirectory attribute capture is implemented at
`9c7c70b8`, with a fixture covering ancestor policy and caller-relative paths.
Full integration verification and retained-request parity remain pending.

## Verification and rollback

Independent fixtures cover chunk boundaries, long lines, match-line limits,
oversized mutations, binary attributes, forced text, custom drivers, immutable
index fallback, policy/configuration mutation, input identity and a no-egress
tripwire. Consulted implementation sources are Entire source and the authorized
plan. Git behavior supplies the existing implementation oracle; no competitor
source or external measurement supplied expectations.

Keep extraction reuse default-off. Disabling it restores the ordinary path.
Temporary policy worktrees are operation-owned and removed on return. A full
end-to-end diagnostic replay and remaining compatibility work are required
before the fixed corpus campaign can resume; no release or speed claim follows
from these fixtures.
package sem

import (
	"context"
	"fmt"
	"strings"

	"github.com/entireio/entire-graph/internal/gitutil"
)

type searchPreselectionScan struct {
	patterns []string
	aliases  []string
	maxLines int
}

func newSearchPreselectionCapture(ctx context.Context, q searchQuery, maxLine int) (*capturePreselectionObserver, error) {
	if len(q.inferredAbbreviations) == 0 {
		return newCapturePreselectionObserver(ctx, searchGitGrepPreselectionPatterns(q), q.terms)
	}
	observer, err := newCaptureSearchPreselectionObserver(ctx, q, maxLine)
	if err != nil {
		// The ordinary alias path treats an unsupported Git expression as a
		// request for the full Go-content fallback. Capture mode must make the
		// same choice rather than rejecting the query before corpus selection.
		return nil, nil
	}
	return observer, nil
}

// searchPreselectionScanPlan is the bounded content plan shared by Git-backed
// and captured working-tree preselection. Ordinary terms share one 32-line
// sample; aliases either share a 32-line sample or get independent first-line
// passes so a common term cannot hide a later abbreviation.
func searchPreselectionScanPlan(q searchQuery) ([]searchPreselectionScan, error) {
	coalesced := len(q.inferredAbbreviations) > 0 && !searchGitAliasScansFit(q)
	primaryTerms := searchGitGrepPreselectionPatterns(q)
	if coalesced {
		primaryTerms = q.terms
	}
	primary := make([]string, 0, len(primaryTerms))
	for _, term := range primaryTerms {
		if !q.inferredAbbreviations[term] {
			primary = append(primary, term)
		}
	}
	plan := make([]searchPreselectionScan, 0, 1+len(q.inferredAbbreviations))
	if len(primary) > 0 {
		patterns := searchGitAliasPatternsForTerms(q, primary)
		if patterns == nil {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("query requires content preselection")
		}
		plan = append(plan, searchPreselectionScan{patterns: patterns, maxLines: 32})
	}
	aliases := make([]string, 0, len(q.inferredAbbreviations))
	for _, term := range q.terms {
		if q.inferredAbbreviations[term] {
			aliases = append(aliases, term)
		}
	}
	if len(aliases) == 0 {
		return plan, nil
	}
	if coalesced {
		patterns := searchGitAliasPatternsForTerms(q, aliases)
		if patterns == nil {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("query requires content preselection")
		}
		return append(plan, searchPreselectionScan{patterns: patterns, aliases: aliases, maxLines: 32}), nil
	}
	for _, alias := range aliases {
		patterns := searchGitAliasPatternsForTerms(q, []string{alias})
		if patterns == nil {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("query requires content preselection")
		}
		plan = append(plan, searchPreselectionScan{patterns: patterns, aliases: []string{alias}, maxLines: 1})
	}
	return plan, nil
}

func capturedSearchPreselectionMatches(
	ctx context.Context,
	source sourceContext,
	tracked []string,
	q searchQuery,
	observer *capturePreselectionObserver,
) ([]gitutil.GrepMatch, int, int, error) {
	observer.activate()
	allowed := make(map[string]bool, len(source.paths))
	for _, path := range source.paths {
		allowed[path] = true
	}
	eligible := make([]string, 0, len(tracked))
	for _, path := range tracked {
		if allowed[path] {
			eligible = append(eligible, path)
		}
	}
	attributes, err := source.capturedDiffAttributes(ctx, eligible)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, 0, len(observer.passes), err
	}

	matches := make([]gitutil.GrepMatch, 0)
	reads := 0
	queryMatcher := newSearchQueryTermMatcher(q)
	for _, path := range tracked {
		if err := ctx.Err(); err != nil {
			return nil, reads, len(observer.passes), err
		}
		if !allowed[path] {
			continue
		}
		content, ok := source.read(path)
		evidence, observed := observer.evidence(path)
		if !observed {
			return nil, reads, len(observer.passes), fmt.Errorf("captured preselection missing evidence for %s", path)
		}
		reads++
		if evidence.err != nil {
			return nil, reads, len(observer.passes), evidence.err
		}
		attribute := attributes[path]
		if attribute.Binary || (!attribute.Text && evidence.binary) {
			continue
		}
		seen := make([]bool, len(q.terms))
		matchedWithoutTerm := false
		for _, passEvidence := range evidence.passes {
			terms := passEvidence.terms
			if passEvidence.needsValidation {
				if !ok {
					return nil, reads, len(observer.passes), fmt.Errorf("captured preselection requires retained content to validate alias in %s", path)
				}
				// Git's conservative alias callback records the complete file even
				// when validation finds no true alias. Preserve the late ordinary
				// evidence and the fully-scanned saturation semantics exactly.
				terms = queryMatcher.match(content)
			}
			for termIndex, matched := range terms {
				seen[termIndex] = seen[termIndex] || matched
			}
			matchedWithoutTerm = matchedWithoutTerm || passEvidence.matched
		}
		emitted := false
		for termIndex, matched := range seen {
			if matched {
				matches = append(matches, gitutil.GrepMatch{Path: path, Text: q.terms[termIndex]})
				emitted = true
			}
		}
		if matchedWithoutTerm && !emitted {
			matches = append(matches, gitutil.GrepMatch{Path: path})
		}
	}
	return matches, reads, len(observer.passes), nil
}

func searchPreselectionAliasConfirmed(q searchQuery, aliases []string, text string) bool {
	lower := strings.ToLower(text)
	for _, alias := range aliases {
		if searchQueryTermMatches(q, text, lower, alias) {
			return true
		}
	}
	return false
}

